  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "Shortwave Radiation Data (J-OFURO)",
  "description": "Japanese Ocean Flux data sets with Use of Remote sensing Observations (J-OFURO) Constructed shorewave radiation data using remote sensing observations. Available are monthly mean and 1 degree by 1 degree grid data over Jan. 1992 - Sep. 2001 and daily mean and 0.25 degree by 0.25 degree grid data. Data variable is solar radiation at the sea surface (W/m 2 ). Data sources include: GMS/VISSR, DMSP/SSMI, NOAA/AVHRR, and TOMS. Data sets are availabe online for download in three file formats: standard ASCII, netCDF, and gzip at http://dtsv.scc.u-tokai.ac.jp/j-ofuro/J-OFURO_SWR.html or anonymous FTP: dtsv.scc.u-tokai.ac.jp/PUB/J-OFURO/SWR/MON. J-OFURO website - http://dtsv.scc.u-tokai.ac.jp/j-ofuro/\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: To derive homogenous data with high resolution using analysis and satellite data for obtaining globally-covered fluxes between ocean and atmosphere.",
